Manage the behaviors per path of a distribution

Usage:
  nexoctl dist behavior [flags]
  nexoctl dist behavior [command]

Available Commands:
  add         Add a behavior for the paths of a pattern
  list        List the behaviors of a distribution, in evaluation order
  move        Move a behavior (1-based positions): the first match wins
  remove      Remove the behavior N (1-based, see behavior ls)

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for behavior

Global Flags:
      --config-dir string   configuration directory (default $NEXOCTL_CONFIG_DIR or ~/.nexoctl)
      --debug               dump the HTTP requests and responses on stderr, with the secrets redacted
      --json                print JSON Lines (one object per line with a "status" member)
      --no-color            disable colors (also with the NO_COLOR environment variable)
  -q, --quiet               hide confirmations and progress (results and errors are still printed)

Use "nexoctl dist behavior [command] --help" for more information about a command.
